# GRRS — Git Repository Scanner

Desktop utility in Odin that recursively discovers Git repositories under a chosen root and displays working-tree and remote-tracking status.

## Locked decisions

- Language: Odin
- Graphics: raylib (`vendor:raylib`) — custom immediate-mode UI
- Git: subprocess via `core:os` `process_exec`; never parse `.git` internals directly
- Concurrency: filesystem scanner + bounded Git worker pool; UI updates on main thread only
- Remote status: branch upstream + local remote-tracking refs; no auto-fetch

## Structure (non-negotiable)

- `src/model/` = shared state, repository types, enums
- `src/app/` = state, actions, main loop wiring
- `src/scanner/` = filesystem discovery
- `src/git/` = git commands, status parsing, repository inspection
- `src/jobs/` = event queue, scan worker orchestration
- `src/ui/` = raylib views, theme, widgets
- `src/platform/` = native folder picker abstraction
- `main.odin` = entry; package `GRRS`

## Style

- Package names match directory names: `app`, `scanner`, `git`, `jobs`, `ui`, `platform`
- Background workers send events; main thread owns `App_State`
- Per-repo Git failures must not abort the scan
